                <pb facs="0591" n="581" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg581"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/3393: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gordon</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-24T16:00:00-04:00">July 24, 1937—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>30. My 29, 7 p.m. Following telegram has been received from American Embassy,
                    Paris: “I discussed yesterday with Delbos and <pb facs="0592" n="582"
                        xml:id="pg582"/> Rochat, director of the American Section of the Foreign
                    Office, the question of French relations with Haiti. Delbos was rather shocked
                    by certain facts which I presented to him and ordered Rochat to investigate the
                    matter thoroughly and give me an explanation today.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
